    <string name="help_vaults">Each vault is separate: its own files, search, tasks and links. The browser switches between them.</string>
    <string name="help_token">A fine-grained token with Contents: read-only on this repository, and nothing else.</string>
    <string name="help_token_rejected">The token was rejected. Fine-grained tokens expire after at most a year &#8212; this one may simply have run out.</string>
    <string name="sync_retry_waiting">Waiting to retry (attempt %1$d)</string>
    <string name="sync_queued">Queued - waiting for the network</string>
    <string name="help_battery">Battery optimisation is on for this app, so Android may defer or skip a scheduled sync indefinitely. Pull to refresh always works.</string>
    <string name="help_digest">Counts what is overdue and due today, from the last sync. Nothing is sent when there is nothing to report.</string>
    <string name="help_transport_rest">Markdown only. A refresh with nothing new costs one request.</string>
    <string name="help_transport_ssh">No token to rotate, but git cannot fetch a subset &#8212; full history and all attachments.</string>
    <string name="help_theme">naz is a dark colourscheme and defines no light palette, so light keeps its accents against paper rather than pretending to be it.</string>
    <string name="help_persian_font">Off uses the platform\'s Naskh, which has every glyph and draws them differently.</string>
    <string name="help_needs_token">Syncing over REST needs an access token. Add one above, or switch that repository to SSH.</string>
    <string name="help_needs_key">%1$s has no SSH key yet. Generate one above and add it to that repository as a read-only deploy key.</string>
    <string name="help_ssh_keys">Every key is generated on this device and its private half never leaves it. What you copy out is the public line, which goes to the repository as a read-only deploy key.</string>
    <string name="help_key_per_repo">GitHub allows a deploy key on exactly one repository, so there is one key per repository rather than one for all of them.</string>
    <string name="help_no_ssh_repo">No repository is set to sync over SSH. Switch one to SSH in Settings and its key will appear here.</string>
    <string name="help_port_443">Many mobile networks block port 22, where a clone simply hangs with no error at all. GitHub answers SSH on 443 too.</string>
    <string name="help_replace_key">The key currently registered on %1$s stops working immediately. Syncing that repository will fail until the new public line is added to it as a deploy key, and the old one should be removed there.</string>
    <string name="help_unused_keys">Left behind by a repository that was removed or switched to REST. Still private keys sitting in the app\'s storage, and the deploy keys they match are probably still registered on GitHub.</string>
